it's taken me a long time to get my head into a state where i feel
comfortable telling y'all about this one, but now i think i'm ready, so here
goes...

this probably has to go down in history as one of the stupidest deaths ever.

you may recall me posting about atalanta the female elven ranger, who had
reached gehennom for the first time (see my post "re: thou art chosen to
take lives for my glory" on 25/04/2004 at 12:18).  well, she progressed
through gehennom, got the candelabrum and book, killed the high priest, took
the amulet, ran for the exit, survived the elemental planes (although i have
no idea how, air and water were total nightmares) and made it to astral.

bear in mind that this was the first time i had ever got a character as far
as *medusa*, and here i was on the astral plane, amulet in hand, wary about
the riders but more f***ing excited than i've been in a computer game for
some time (ever, probably).  I decided to head towards the left and was soon
approached by pestilence.  i zapped him with my wand of death.  and what did
i do next?

** ATE HIS CORPSE**

now, i have spent the last three days or so trying to figure out why on
earth i would do a thing like that.  and you know what?  i was totally
convinced, at the time, that i had just killed famine.  i was bothered about
starvation if he came back (i'd left most of my food behind).  i thought
"let's try to kill two birds with one stone - if i eat him, it'll stave off
hunger and keep him out of my way for a while".  with hindsight, probably
eating the corpse of famine would have been just as fatal as eating the
corpse of pestilence, but so much for hindsight.  i guess the mind works in
some messed up ways when the adrenaline's pumping.

so, the "yafap" will have to wait.  at least now i feel better prepared for
another shot.  lessons learned (apart from the obvious):

1. don't enter the planes without a means of finding the portals.  i only
had one potion of booze to confuse myself, and spent ages on fire, air and
water finding the damn ^s

2. have plenty of amulets of life saving - those air elementals are *nasty*

3. it's possible to get a *very* long way with a ranger at "basic" in bow
and without casting a single spell

4. gehennom is a pain without a light source...

